# Editor UI copy

Write labels, helper text, and section blurbs for **authors and designers**, not for plugin/runtime internals.

## Do

- Describe **what the field does** in plain language (“How long this state lasts on the map.”).
- Use **game terms** the author already knows (map, battler, expires, bonus, frames when the field is frames).
- Keep section intros to **one short sentence** when needed at all.
- Use status lines that reflect **outcome** (“Does not expire on the map.” / “Expires on the map ~60s.”).

## Do not

- Explain **J-ABS**, **RMMZ**, **MZ**, `removeByWalking`, `stepsToRemove`, or why the engine behaves a certain way.
- Put **notetag names** in labels, checkboxes, or `helperText` (`<stateDuration:N>`, “writes …”, etc.).
- Use **Runtime:**, **J-ABS reads**, or other developer-facing phrasing.
- Duplicate the accordion title with a long subtitle that says the same thing.

## Tone

Same bar as in-game skill/state descriptions: useful to someone balancing content, not someone reading source code. If a sentence would feel wrong on a Final Fantasy ability screen, it does not belong in this editor.
